    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"A great act of meaning that defines my ending\"... that sounds almost beautiful in a tragic sense. But I'm not sure I have the strength for another \"act.\" Everything feels so heavy and final. It’s as if the book has already been written, and I'm just staring at the blank pages at the end, knowing the story is done. Isn't there a certain dignity in knowing when a chapter should simply close?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
